## I1 resolved and focused breakage assessment

- `review-freeze-02/operations.py:680-686` retains the original persisted campaign start and configured duration when deriving the operational monotonic deadline. This expression is unchanged; the correction neither restarts nor extends the deadline.
- `operations.py:707-715` authenticates immutable settled facts first, then returns `campaign_deadline_exhausted` when the original operational deadline has expired, before evaluating the target/reserve decision at `:716`. It therefore handles an already-expired resume and expiry during heavy fact authentication. Integrity failures still propagate before deadline/target handling. Clock access stays in the operational closure; shared admission source is byte-identical.
- Reused settlements consume this decision at `operations.py:763-767`; newly completed settlements consume it at `:967-971`. Both retain the deadline reason and break, including when the current round is the final permitted iteration. Neither can convert this returned reason into the target result. Pre-config and pre-start consumers at `:792-798` and `:890-896` accept the same reason and preserve their existing additional checks.
- `operations.py:985-988` maps only `max_feedback_rounds` and `evaluated_feedback_target_reached` to outer `completed`, so the new deadline result remains outer `stopped`. The old summary call/readiness/count formulas are unchanged. No synthetic outcome or record is introduced.
- Legacy absence returns at `operations.py:705-706` before the added clock check. The exact two-line scope and unchanged CLI/admission bytes preserve the prior reviewed contracts and immutable call paths. No new breakage was identified within this delta.

